    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d86">

                <pb facs="0112" n="102" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/3394: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-23T16:00:00+07:00">August 23, 1943—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 23—3:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1547. Chungking was raided this morning by some 22 Japanese planes which flew
                    over the city but apparently dropped bombs only in the outskirts near a small
                    arsenal. Some defense by Chinese planes. While Japanese reconnaissance planes
                    have come over occasionally, this is first actual raid since September 1941.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
